.TH DTERROR.DS 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dterror.ds \- show an error dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dterror.ds
.I message
.RI [ title
.RI [ button ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dterror.ds
shows
.I message
in an error dialog, with
.I title
as the window's title and one button labelled
.I button
(OK when not given), and exits when the button is pressed.
Programs and scripts use it to report an error where they cannot show a
dialog themselves: after a failed
.BR exec (2)
in a child process, or before their main window exists.
.BR dtfile (1)
and
.BR dtopen (1)
call it.
.SH NOTES
.B dterror.ds
is a
.B dtksh
script.
.B dtksh
is not yet part of this package, so the script does not run and its
callers' errors go unseen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtfile (1),
.BR dtopen (1)
